Net-SNMP provides native Windows libraries; link netsnmp and the required
agent libraries from lib (Release) or debug/lib (Debug).

Runtime data:
  Keep share/snmp with the deployed application. Net-SNMP searches for
  share/snmp/mibs beside its DLL (or executable for static linkage), then
  one and two directories above it. This supports vcpkg's bin, debug/bin,
  and tools/net-snmp layouts without depending on the working directory.
  Custom layouts can use netsnmp_set_mib_directory() before init_mib(), or
  the upstream MIBDIRS setting. Configuration defaults follow the same root.

Writable state:
  Persistent state defaults to %LOCALAPPDATA%/net-snmp/persist, separately
  from the installation. LOCALAPPDATA must be an absolute drive-letter path.
  Services and applications needing separate state should set
  SNMP_PERSISTENT_DIR to their own absolute writable directory, or call
  netsnmp_ds_set_string(NETSNMP_DS_LIBRARY_ID, NETSNMP_DS_LIB_PERSISTENT_DIR,
                        absolute_path) before init_snmp().
  Use SNMPCONFPATH or the NETSNMP_DS_LIB_CONFIGURATION_DIR string setting
  for application-specific configuration.
  Temporary files use the Windows temporary directory.

C++ consumers of this upstream version must include standard C++ headers
before Net-SNMP headers, which define the inline keyword as a macro.
